Hi:

We're an IT Security company based in Canberra Australia. We've been =
looking at (but yet to experiment with) the Security-Enhanced Linux =
distribution, which the NSA recently published. We were somewhat =
surprised that this distribution does not _appear_ to have any extended =
logging or auditing functions, in the same way as other C2 compliant O/S =
have, such as Win NT Event Logging, Solaris BSM, AIX, etc. Is planned to =
have a audit module included in "selinux"?

We had some ideas about including a "BSM style" audit module for Linux, =
as seen in our press release: =
http://www.intersectalliance.com/news/index2.html#02032000 However, =
other pressing matters have precluded us from undertaking this work, at =
the present time.


